{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_3e6c1ef8f5ff",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 741,
      "mechanism": "Reverses wb_data byte order on writes to FIFO A/B address lanes (SDSPI_FIFO_A_ADDR and SDSPI_FIFO_B_ADDR) via the same wb_data bus path that feeds command/data registers. This is the only patch editing the multi-lane FIFO write data path, matching the observed o_mosi bit-flip pattern at cycle 484124+ where SPI output diverges due to misordered FIFO content."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_29d173398429",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 770,
      "mechanism": "Reverses wb_data byte order only for FIFO B writes (SDSPI_FIFO_B_ADDR). Complements patch_3e6c1ef8f5ff by covering the second FIFO lane; the o_mosi failures occur during a sequence exercising both FIFO address spaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_60defe19ec35",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 164,
      "mechanism": "Reverses wb_data byte order at the Wishbone register capture point (r_wb_data). Since the same data bus feeds CMD, DAT, and FIFO address writes, this edit propagates reversed byte order into r_data_reg and FIFO memories, directly altering the serial bit stream emitted on o_mosi."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_15ae8a9243d8",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 305,
      "mechanism": "Adds pre_cmd_state qualification to the r_cmd_state==3'h1 transition. The trace shows pre_cmd_state toggling at the exact cycles (484118-484127) where o_mosi first diverges; gating the command-byte emission on this pulse aligns the state machine with the bus-cycle qualification required by the testbench."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_98a3b7158151",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 327,
      "mechanism": "Qualifies the r_cmd_state==3'h5 transition with r_use_fifo. The failing window includes i_wb_data[11] (r_use_fifo) toggling at cycle 484119-484127, so gating the FIFO-read startup path on this flag prevents premature SPI transactions that corrupt o_mosi."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_0ce0a636b1ee",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 334,
      "mechanism": "Changes the FIFO-read launch condition from (r_use_fifo && r_fifo_wr) to (r_use_fifo && r_fifo_wr && ll_fifo_rd_complete). The observed mismatch burst starts when a FIFO read would begin before the prior read completes; requiring completion eliminates the overlap that drives o_mosi off-sequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_171aea9942d8",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 334,
      "mechanism": "Changes the same FIFO-read launch condition to (r_use_fifo && r_fifo_wr && r_have_resp). Since r_have_resp rises only after a valid response token, this ensures the SPI read transaction starts only when the card is ready, matching the cycle-exact bus protocol."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_70dca1511670",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 337,
      "mechanism": "Qualifies the r_cmd_state==3'h6 transition with r_fifo_wr (instead of r_use_fifo). The failing trace shows r_fifo_wr toggling in the same window; gating the SPI write-continue state on the actual write-direction flag prevents state-machine desynchronization that corrupts o_mosi."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The 4032-cycle o_mosi mismatch burst beginning at cycle 484124 coincides with a Wishbone write sequence that exercises both FIFO A and FIFO B address lanes while toggling r_use_fifo, r_fifo_wr, and pre_cmd_state. Patches that reverse the byte order on the wb_data bus (patch_3e6c1ef8f5ff, patch_29d173398429, patch_60defe19ec35) directly address the most visible symptom—bit-order inversion on the serial output. Patches that add the missing pre_cmd_state, r_use_fifo, r_fifo_wr, and response-completion qualifications to the command-state transitions (patch_15ae8a9243d8, patch_98a3b7158151, patch_0ce0a636b1ee, patch_171aea9942d8, patch_70dca1511670) correct the cycle-exact state-machine pacing that the testbench expects. Together these eight edits cover the FIFO data path, the bus-cycle qualification pulse, and the response-token handshake observed in the failing trace window."
}
